{
  "donor_id": "NanmiCoder--MediaCrawler",
  "commit_sha": "bf28178082bc69989954f65a13a17bc129b9aa6e",
  "license": "NON-COMMERCIAL-LEARNING-1.1: clean-room only, nothing copied",
  "method": "every first-party file reviewed by a read-only review (platform clients, login, signing and core modules read in detail; console and docs by purpose); slider-CAPTCHA solving, the dummy x-tt-argus gateway header and the cross-process SMS cache were spot-checked against the source",
  "findings": [
    "Every platform crawler forces a logged-in session (QR, phone/SMS or cookie capture) when a probe fails; data is in practice fetched logged in",
    "Circumvention throughout: stealth scripts and AutomationControlled disabling, real-browser CDP attach, automated slider-CAPTCHA solving (OpenCV Canny + matchTemplate, eased drag trajectories), re-implemented or hooked request signatures (x-s, a_bogus, x-zse-96, WBI, __NS_hxfalcon), a dummy x-tt-argus header to pass an edge gateway, fake navigation paths and in-browser fetches to avoid TLS blocking, proxy rotation against IP bans",
    "Non-circumvention patterns of value: comment trees flattened with parent ids and sub-comment counts, four cursor styles with a repeated-offset stall guard, date-sliced search with per-day quotas, jittered backoff on explicit throttle codes with non-retryable error classes, keyword-provenance tagging of stored posts, offline HTML fixtures for parser regression",
    "Defects: CJK abbreviated counts (1.2万) lose their unit, the creator hash is unsalted and linkable, and the SMS relay cannot reach the login loop because each process has its own memory cache"
  ],
